   "name": "Absolute value",
   "requires": [
    "math.integer-signs"
   ],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero, so it is never negative. We write it with two bars. |5| = 5 and |−5| = 5, because both are 5 steps from zero. For a negative x, |x| = −x, which is positive."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "የቁጥር ፍጹም ዋጋ ከዜሮ ያለው ርቀት ነው፤ ስለዚህ አሉታዊ አይሆንም። በሁለት ቋሚ መስመሮች እንጽፈዋለን። |5| = 5 እና |−5| = 5 ነው፤ ሁለቱም ከዜሮ 5 እርምጃ ይርቃሉ።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
